<component type="desktop-application">
  <id>io.github.blackbird410.TrussAnalysis</id>
  <metadata_license>MIT</metadata_license>
  <project_license>MIT</project_license>
  <name>2D Truss Analysis</name>
  <summary>Professional 2D truss structural analysis software</summary>

  <description>
    <p>
      2D Truss Analysis is a professional-grade structural analysis application built with
      modern C++20 and Qt6, featuring an interactive drawing canvas and a robust
      computational engine for analysing 2D truss structures.
    </p>
    <p>Key features:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Interactive drawing canvas with mouse-based node and member placement</li>
      <li>Direct stiffness method (displacement method) implementation</li>
      <li>Support for various load types and boundary conditions</li>
      <li>Comprehensive results tables: reactions, displacements, member forces</li>
      <li>Visual deformation plots and axial force diagrams</li>
      <li>Material and cross-section property management</li>
      <li>Export to CSV, JSON, XML, HTML, LaTeX, and plain text</li>
      <li>Dark and light themes</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      This tool is invaluable for Civil Engineering students and professionals,
      helping validate manual calculations and providing insight into structural behaviour.
    </p>
  </description>

  <launchable type="desktop-id">truss-analysis.desktop</launchable>

